            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This completely invalidates the \"autoload-in-lua\" approach (and even adds ~2ms overhead on top of that). If the `enable()` call is not not deferred (e.g., in an autocommand callback or mapping rhs), it's better to just inline the code here.\n\n(Individual functions -- especially ones that are not called unconditionally -- can still live in `lua/nvim/`.)",
            "commit_id": "c65b4f55683a78c8eddbf6f1e26c9e674af4bb87",
            "created_at": "2026-07-09T23:08:28Z",
