        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "IIRC the original suggestion was to let these live in parallel at least for a while -- if people can opt-in to the legacy implementation, that removes pressure from us to keep bug-for-bug compatibility in the rewrite. Personally, I'd prefer a sane \"reboot\" as long as the differences are not serious regressions. (Insert spacebar heating meme here.)\r\n\r\n(As `matchit` is enabled by default in Neovim, the new implementation can live in the standard runtime, freeing the `pack/opt` for keeping the legacy plugin -- with an added disabling of the Lua plugin. This allows us to keep the oldtest, too.)\r\n\r\nI'm fine with common code reuse being a {soonish) follow-up step; I just wanted to raise the point (and hear whether there are fundamental issues preventing code reuse at all).",
            "created_at": "2026-07-09T23:23:09Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40664#issuecomment-4930443858",
            "id": 4930443858,
